{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-162346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $z$ and $w$ be $4$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${w}^{4}+1=1$\n- ${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1$\n- $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ and $w$ are $4$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{4}={w}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n{w}^{4}+1=1+1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4} & =\\frac{{z}^{4}}{{w}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that ${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1,$ which means that $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the quotient of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad9d2f63f389d84e1fd4291612724ab1645baa288edc371e9fb062bdc7908fbf"} {"question" "q-162346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $z$ be a $6$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $({z}^{3})^{2}=-1$\n- ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity\n- ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{2}={z}^{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{6} & =({z}^{6})^{3} \\\\  & =(1)^{3} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement I, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{3})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad9d2f63f389d84e1fd4291612724ab1645baa288edc371e9fb062bdc7908fbf"} {"question" "q-162347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $z$ be a $4$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${z}^{4}=-1$\n- $(z+z)^{4}=16$\n- $z+z=2z$  is not a $4$th root of unity" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ is a  $4$th root of unity, then (by definition) we have that\n\n$$\n{z}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+z)^{4} & =(2z)^{4} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}\\cdot {z}^{4} \\\\  & =16\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that $(z+z)^{4}\\ne 1,$ which means that $z+z=2z$ is *not* a $4$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad9d2f63f389d84e1fd4291612724ab1645baa288edc371e9fb062bdc7908fbf"} {"question" "q-162368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-162368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-281256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The sum of all nine $9$th roots of unity is equal to$\\,$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-281256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the principal $9$th root of unity is \n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/9}\\ne 1,\n$$\n\nand that any $9$th root of unity is of the form ${z}^{k}$ for $k=0,1,...,8.$  Also, we have ${z}^{9}=1.$\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of a geometric sequence, we obtain that the sum of all eight roots is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+z+{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}+{z}^{4}+{z}^{5}+{z}^{6}+{z}^{7}+{z}^{8} & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-{z}^{9})}{1-z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-1)}{1-z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0}{1-z} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-281256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad9d2f63f389d84e1fd4291612724ab1645baa288edc371e9fb062bdc7908fbf"} {"question" "q-281256" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-281256" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-319771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The product of all sixteen $16$th roots of unity is equal to$\\,$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-319771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the principal $16$th root of unity is \n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/16}={e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/8},\n$$\n\nand that any $16$th root of unity is of the form ${z}^{k}$ for $k=0,1,...,15.$ Also, we have ${z}^{16}=1.$\n\nTherefore, the product of all sixteen roots is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{0}\\cdot {z}^{1}\\cdot {z}^{2}\\cdot {z}^{3}\\cdot {z}^{4}\\cdot {z}^{5}\\cdot {z}^{6}\\cdot {z}^{7}\\cdot {z}^{8}\\cdot {z}^{9}\\cdot {z}^{10}\\cdot {z}^{11}\\cdot {z}^{12}\\cdot {z}^{13}\\cdot {z}^{14}\\cdot {z}^{15} & ={z}^{0\\,+\\,1\\,+\\,2\\,+\\,3\\,+\\,4\\,+\\,5\\,+\\,6+\\,⋯+15} \\\\  & ={z}^{120} \\\\  & ={z}^{112+8} \\\\  & ={z}^{112}\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & ={({z}^{16})}^{7}\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & =1\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & ={z}^{8} \\\\  & ={({e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/8})}^{8} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi \\text{i}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-319771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad9d2f63f389d84e1fd4291612724ab1645baa288edc371e9fb062bdc7908fbf"} {"question" "q-319771" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"} {"question" "q-319771" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056353/state.json" "file_sha256" "6745052af43f341529019a1a246007284cc5e0aba3486fc8dd141aaa917b99a2"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1902 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
